== General Description ==

The '''Fender Reverb Unit''' (6G15) was a tube, spring reverb-equipped effects unit made by [[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fender_Musical_Instrument_Corporation|Fender]]. The Reverb Unit was originally introduced in 1961. It was discontinued in 1966 and was replaced by a solid-state model, the FR1000.^[[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fender_Reverb_Unit#cite_note-1|[1]]]^ The unit features three controls: Dwell, Mix and Tone and is run by two pre-amp tubes and a power tube. Physically the unit looks like a small ampilfier head and since the early '60s the unit has become synonymous with surf music.

